%% title: `CLI Bootstrap State Machine`
%% summary: Same-host caller bootstrap before a daemon request is sent.
%% commentary: CliComposition::bootstrap resolves the account-scoped endpoint and constructs a Tokio HTTP client. The managed daemon lifecycle is separate; bootstrap does not launch a daemon.
%% notes: endpoint resolution and client construction are code-owned | a configured client does not prove daemon availability
%% recovery_rules: If endpoint resolution or client construction fails, return the typed error. | A later request reports connection failures through the client transport.
%% terminal_classes: BootstrapFailed is a caller-facing typed error. | ClientConfigured allows the command to issue a request.
%% sets: daemon
flowchart TD
    A["BootstrapPending<br/>caller entered CliComposition::bootstrap()"] --> B["ResolveAccountEndpoint"]
    B -->|resolution_error| E["BootstrapFailed<br/>caller: typed error"]
    B -->|endpoint_resolved| C["ConstructLocalHttpClient"]
    C -->|configuration_error| E
    C -->|client_configured| S["ClientConfigured<br/>caller: may issue request"]

    classDef happy fill:#14532d,color:#ffffff,stroke:#14532d,stroke-width:2px;
    classDef error fill:#7f1d1d,color:#ffffff,stroke:#7f1d1d,stroke-width:2px;
    classDef neutral fill:#e2e8f0,color:#111827,stroke:#334155,stroke-width:2px;

    class A,S happy;
    class E error;
    class B,C neutral;
